--
-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: the capacities, powers and offices the Act gives or
-- implies (ss 17, 19, 21, 22, 23, 27 and 41).
-- Pass 2. A rule is a function over the thing asked about (what a corporation might do, who a minister's name includes,
-- what a regulation-making power is construed to cover) and the facts that bear on it. Where the text lists what a
-- power "includes" or what a corporation "may do", the list is open: an item not on it is a refusal, not FALSE
-- (NOTES.md, fork F-open-list).
--
-- What FALSE and REFUSE mean here (NOTES.md, finding 2). TRUE: the case is within the provision and the provision gives the
-- thing. FALSE: only where the words of the provision give the negative themselves (an exception, "is not", "must ... one
-- whose"). REFUSE: the case is outside what the provision speaks of, or the provision only permits or "includes" and the
-- case is not listed; the text is silent and a default would be a guess.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude

§ `s 17 Corporate rights and powers`

DECLARE `Something a corporation might do` IS ONE OF
    `Sue and be sued in its corporate name`
    `Contract and be contracted with in its corporate name`
    `Have a common seal, and alter or change it`
    `Acquire or dispose of property`
        HAS `the property is land`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
            `it is for the corporation's purposes`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `Regulate its own procedure and business`
    `Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals`
        HAS `its name consists of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Do something else`

-- src:97 | 17 (1) A corporation has perpetual succession and may do the following:
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(1) (src:97)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) a corporation has perpetual succession` MEANS TRUE

-- src:97 | 17 (1) A corporation has perpetual succession and may do the following:
-- src:98 | (a) sue and be sued in its corporate name;
-- src:99 | (b) contract and be contracted with in its corporate name;
-- src:100 | (c) have a common seal and may alter or change it;
-- src:101 | (d) acquire and dispose of property other than land for its purposes;
-- src:102 | (e) regulate its own procedure and business;
-- src:103 | (f) in the case of a corporation with a name consisting of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form, use either the English or French form of its name or both forms and show on its seal both the English and French forms of its name or have 2 seals, one showing the English and the other showing the French form of its name.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(1) (src:97-103)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else"

-- src:97 | 17 (1) A corporation has perpetual succession and may do the following:
-- src:98 | (a) sue and be sued in its corporate name;
-- src:99 | (b) contract and be contracted with in its corporate name;
-- src:100 | (c) have a common seal and may alter or change it;
-- src:101 | (d) acquire and dispose of property other than land for its purposes;
-- src:102 | (e) regulate its own procedure and business;
-- src:103 | (f) in the case of a corporation with a name consisting of an English and a French form or a combined English and French form, use either the English or French form of its name or both forms and show on its seal both the English and French forms of its name or have 2 seals, one showing the English and the other showing the French form of its name.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(1)(a) to (f) (src:97-103)
GIVEN thing IS A `Something a corporation might do`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) a corporation may do the thing` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `Sue and be sued in its corporate name` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Contract and be contracted with in its corporate name` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Have a common seal, and alter or change it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Acquire or dispose of property` isLand forPurposes THEN
            IF   (NOT isLand) AND forPurposes
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else`
        WHEN `Regulate its own procedure and business` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Use either form of its name or both, and show both forms on its seal or have 2 seals` bilingual THEN
            IF   bilingual
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE `s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else`
        WHEN `Do something else` THEN `s 17(1) lists what a corporation may do and does not say it may do nothing else`

-- src:104 | (2) A majority of the members of the corporation may bind the others and the corporation by their acts.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(2) (src:104)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do"

-- src:104 | (2) A majority of the members of the corporation may bind the others and the corporation by their acts.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(2) (src:104)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) is not given a number acting that is more than the number of members` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(2) is not given a number acting that is more than the number of members"

-- "A majority" is read as more than half: the Act does not define the word (NOTES.md, finding 9).
-- src:104 | (2) A majority of the members of the corporation may bind the others and the corporation by their acts.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(2) (src:104)
GIVEN `the number of members of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who act`               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(2) the members who act may bind the others and the corporation` `the number of members of the corporation` `the number of them who act` MEANS
    IF   `the number of them who act` GREATER THAN `the number of members of the corporation`
    THEN `s 17(2) is not given a number acting that is more than the number of members`
    ELSE IF 2 TIMES `the number of them who act` GREATER THAN `the number of members of the corporation`
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE `s 17(2) says what a majority of the members may do and does not say what fewer may do`

-- src:105 | (3) Individual members of a corporation established by an enactment who do not contravene the enactment are exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(3) (src:105)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation"

-- src:105 | (3) Individual members of a corporation established by an enactment who do not contravene the enactment are exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 17(3) (src:105)
GIVEN `the corporation is established by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member contravenes the enactment`           IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(3) the member is exempt from personal liability for the corporation's debts, obligations or acts` `the corporation is established by an enactment` `the member contravenes the enactment` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation is established by an enactment` AND (NOT `the member contravenes the enactment`)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 17(3) speaks only of a member who does not contravene the enactment that established the corporation`

§ `s 19 Powers to judges and court officers`

DECLARE `Who holds a power given by an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `A judge of a court`
    `An officer of a court`
    `Someone else`

-- src:116 | 19 (1) If by an enactment judicial or quasi judicial powers are given to a judge or officer of a court, the judge or officer in exercising the powers does so in the judge's or officer's official capacity and representing the court.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 19(1) (src:116)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court"

-- src:116 | 19 (1) If by an enactment judicial or quasi judicial powers are given to a judge or officer of a court, the judge or officer in exercising the powers does so in the judge's or officer's official capacity and representing the court.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 19(1) (src:116)
GIVEN holder IS A `Who holds a power given by an enactment`
      `the power is given by an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is judicial or quasi judicial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the holder exercises the power in the holder's official capacity and represents the court` holder `the power is given by an enactment` `the power is judicial or quasi judicial` MEANS
    IF   `the power is given by an enactment` AND `the power is judicial or quasi judicial`
    THEN CONSIDER holder
             WHEN `A judge of a court` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `An officer of a court` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Someone else` THEN `s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court`
    ELSE `s 19(1) speaks only of judicial or quasi judicial powers given by an enactment to a judge or officer of a court`

-- src:117 | (2) Without restricting subsection (1), if under an enactment an appeal is given from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge, an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge as in the case of any other proceeding in that court or in the court of which the judge is a member.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 19(2) (src:117)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) speaks only of an appeal given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 19(2) speaks only of an appeal given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge"

-- src:117 | (2) Without restricting subsection (1), if under an enactment an appeal is given from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge, an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge as in the case of any other proceeding in that court or in the court of which the judge is a member.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 19(2) (src:117)
GIVEN `an appeal is given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) an appeal lies from the decision of the court or judge as in any other proceeding in that court` `an appeal is given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge` MEANS
    IF   `an appeal is given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 19(2) speaks only of an appeal given under an enactment from a person, board, commission or other body to a court or judge`

§ `s 21 Demise of the Crown`

-- The three sentences of s 21 about a person who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign.
-- src:132 | 21 On a demise of the Crown, it is not necessary to renew a commission or appointment by which a person in British Columbia held or exercised their office or profession during the previous reign, but all persons who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign continue in the exercise of the duties and functions of their respective offices and professions as fully as if newly appointed by commission or appointment from the Sovereign for the time being from the date of the Sovereign's accession, and it is not necessary for those persons to take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 21 (src:132)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown"

-- src:132 | 21 On a demise of the Crown, it is not necessary to renew a commission or appointment by which a person in British Columbia held or exercised their office or profession during the previous reign, but all persons who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign continue in the exercise of the duties and functions of their respective offices and professions as fully as if newly appointed by commission or appointment from the Sovereign for the time being from the date of the Sovereign's accession, and it is not necessary for those persons to take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 21 (src:132)
GIVEN `a demise of the Crown has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21 the commission or appointment must be renewed` `a demise of the Crown has occurred` `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` MEANS
    IF   `a demise of the Crown has occurred` AND `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown`

-- src:132 | 21 On a demise of the Crown, it is not necessary to renew a commission or appointment by which a person in British Columbia held or exercised their office or profession during the previous reign, but all persons who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign continue in the exercise of the duties and functions of their respective offices and professions as fully as if newly appointed by commission or appointment from the Sovereign for the time being from the date of the Sovereign's accession, and it is not necessary for those persons to take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 21 (src:132)
GIVEN `a demise of the Crown has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21 the person continues in the duties and functions of the office or profession` `a demise of the Crown has occurred` `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` MEANS
    IF   `a demise of the Crown has occurred` AND `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown`

-- src:132 | 21 On a demise of the Crown, it is not necessary to renew a commission or appointment by which a person in British Columbia held or exercised their office or profession during the previous reign, but all persons who held or exercised an office or profession under the late Sovereign continue in the exercise of the duties and functions of their respective offices and professions as fully as if newly appointed by commission or appointment from the Sovereign for the time being from the date of the Sovereign's accession, and it is not necessary for those persons to take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 21 (src:132)
GIVEN `a demise of the Crown has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21 the person must take an oath of allegiance to the new Sovereign` `a demise of the Crown has occurred` `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign` MEANS
    IF   `a demise of the Crown has occurred` AND `the person held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `s 21 speaks only of a person who held or exercised an office or profession in British Columbia during the previous reign, on a demise of the Crown`

§ `s 22 Included powers`

DECLARE `A power over a public officer` IS ONE OF
    `Set the public officer's term of office`
    `Terminate the public officer's appointment, or remove or suspend the public officer`
    `Reappoint or reinstate the public officer`
    `Set the public officer's remuneration, and vary or terminate it`
    `Appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place`
    `Appoint a person as the public officer's deputy`
    `Another power over the public officer`

-- src:135 | 22 Words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer include power to do the following:
-- src:136 | (a) set the public officer's term of office;
-- src:137 | (b) terminate the public officer's appointment or remove or suspend the public officer;
-- src:138 | (c) reappoint or reinstate the public officer;
-- src:139 | (d) set the public officer's remuneration and vary or terminate it;
-- src:140 | (e) appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place;
-- src:141 | (f) appoint a person as the public officer's deputy.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 22 (src:135-141)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22 speaks only of words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 22 speaks only of words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer"

-- src:135 | 22 Words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer include power to do the following:
-- src:136 | (a) set the public officer's term of office;
-- src:137 | (b) terminate the public officer's appointment or remove or suspend the public officer;
-- src:138 | (c) reappoint or reinstate the public officer;
-- src:139 | (d) set the public officer's remuneration and vary or terminate it;
-- src:140 | (e) appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place;
-- src:141 | (f) appoint a person as the public officer's deputy.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 22 (src:135-141)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22 lists the powers such words include and does not say they include no others` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 22 lists the powers such words include and does not say they include no others"

-- src:135 | 22 Words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer include power to do the following:
-- src:136 | (a) set the public officer's term of office;
-- src:137 | (b) terminate the public officer's appointment or remove or suspend the public officer;
-- src:138 | (c) reappoint or reinstate the public officer;
-- src:139 | (d) set the public officer's remuneration and vary or terminate it;
-- src:140 | (e) appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place;
-- src:141 | (f) appoint a person as the public officer's deputy.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 22(a) to (f) (src:135-141)
GIVEN power IS A `A power over a public officer`
      `the words authorize the appointment of a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22 words authorizing the appointment of a public officer include the power` power `the words authorize the appointment of a public officer` MEANS
    IF   `the words authorize the appointment of a public officer`
    THEN CONSIDER power
             WHEN `Set the public officer's term of office` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Terminate the public officer's appointment, or remove or suspend the public officer` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Reappoint or reinstate the public officer` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Set the public officer's remuneration, and vary or terminate it` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Appoint another in the public officer's place or to act in the public officer's place` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Appoint a person as the public officer's deputy` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Another power over the public officer` THEN `s 22 lists the powers such words include and does not say they include no others`
    ELSE `s 22 speaks only of words in an enactment authorizing the appointment of a public officer`

§ `s 23 Powers to act for ministers, deputy ministers and public officers`

DECLARE `Who the words naming a minister include` IS ONE OF
    `A minister designated to act in the office`
    `The deputy of the minister`
    `The associate deputy of the minister`
    `Someone else`

-- src:144 | 23 (1) Words in an enactment directing or empowering a minister of the government to do something, or otherwise applying to the minister by the minister's name of office, include a minister designated to act in the office and the deputy or associate deputy of the minister.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(1) (src:144)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) lists whom words naming a minister include and does not say they include no one else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 23(1) lists whom words naming a minister include and does not say they include no one else"

-- 23 (5): subsection (1) does not authorize a deputy or an associate deputy to enact a regulation as defined in the
-- Regulations Act. The minister designated to act is not named in (5), so the designated minister keeps the authority.
-- src:144 | 23 (1) Words in an enactment directing or empowering a minister of the government to do something, or otherwise applying to the minister by the minister's name of office, include a minister designated to act in the office and the deputy or associate deputy of the minister.
-- src:148 | (5) Subsection (1) does not authorize a deputy or an associate deputy of a minister to exercise an authority conferred on the minister to enact a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(1) and (5) (src:144, src:148)
GIVEN who IS A `Who the words naming a minister include`
      `the authority is to enact a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the words naming a minister include` who `the authority is to enact a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
        WHEN `A minister designated to act in the office` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The deputy of the minister` THEN NOT `the authority is to enact a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act`
        WHEN `The associate deputy of the minister` THEN NOT `the authority is to enact a regulation as defined in the Regulations Act`
        WHEN `Someone else` THEN `s 23(1) lists whom words naming a minister include and does not say they include no one else`

DECLARE `Who steps in for a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act` IS ONE OF
    `An assistant deputy minister`
        HAS `the minister has authorized the assistant deputy minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Some other official authorized by the minister`
    `Some other official not authorized by the minister`

-- src:145 | (2) If a deputy minister is absent or unable to act, an assistant deputy minister, or some other official authorized by the minister, has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(2) (src:145)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) speaks only of a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 23(2) speaks only of a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act"

-- src:145 | (2) If a deputy minister is absent or unable to act, an assistant deputy minister, or some other official authorized by the minister, has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(2) (src:145)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) names an assistant deputy minister or an official authorized by the minister and no one else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 23(2) names an assistant deputy minister or an official authorized by the minister and no one else"

-- Fork F-adm: does "authorized by the minister" qualify "some other official" only, or "an assistant deputy minister" as
-- well? This function takes the first reading: an assistant deputy minister steps in whether or not the minister has
-- authorized that assistant deputy minister. The second reading is asserted, to fail, in `bc-tests-alt-readings-2-expected-fail.l4`.
-- src:145 | (2) If a deputy minister is absent or unable to act, an assistant deputy minister, or some other official authorized by the minister, has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(2) (src:145)
GIVEN who IS A `Who steps in for a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act`
      `the deputy minister is absent or unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the official has the powers and must perform the duties of the deputy minister` who `the deputy minister is absent or unable to act` MEANS
    IF   `the deputy minister is absent or unable to act`
    THEN CONSIDER who
             WHEN `An assistant deputy minister` authorized THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Some other official authorized by the minister` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Some other official not authorized by the minister` THEN `s 23(2) names an assistant deputy minister or an official authorized by the minister and no one else`
    ELSE `s 23(2) speaks only of a deputy minister who is absent or unable to act`

DECLARE `Who the words naming a public officer include` IS ONE OF
    `A person acting for the public officer`
    `A person appointed to act in the office`
    `The deputy of the public officer`
    `Someone else`

-- src:146 | (3) Words in an enactment directing or empowering a public officer to do something, or otherwise applying to the public officer by the public officer's name of office, include a person acting for the public officer or appointed to act in the office and the deputy of the public officer.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(3) (src:146)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) lists whom words naming a public officer include and does not say they include no one else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 23(3) lists whom words naming a public officer include and does not say they include no one else"

-- src:146 | (3) Words in an enactment directing or empowering a public officer to do something, or otherwise applying to the public officer by the public officer's name of office, include a person acting for the public officer or appointed to act in the office and the deputy of the public officer.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(3) (src:146)
GIVEN who IS A `Who the words naming a public officer include`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) the words naming a public officer include` who MEANS
    CONSIDER who
        WHEN `A person acting for the public officer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A person appointed to act in the office` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The deputy of the public officer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Someone else` THEN `s 23(3) lists whom words naming a public officer include and does not say they include no one else`

-- src:147 | (4) This section applies whether or not the office of a minister or public officer is vacant.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 23(4) (src:147)
GIVEN `the office of the minister or public officer is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) section 23 applies` `the office of the minister or public officer is vacant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the office of the minister or public officer is vacant`
        WHEN TRUE THEN TRUE
        WHEN FALSE THEN TRUE

§ `s 27 Ancillary powers`

DECLARE `Kind of official a thing is to be done by or before` IS ONE OF
    `A judge`
    `A justice`
    `A coroner`
    `A public officer`
    `Another kind of person`

-- src:207 | 27 (1) If in an enactment anything is required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer, it must be done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(1) (src:207)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer"

-- src:207 | 27 (1) If in an enactment anything is required or authorized to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer, it must be done by or before one whose jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(1) (src:207)
GIVEN official IS A `Kind of official a thing is to be done by or before`
      `an enactment requires or authorizes the thing to be done by or before that kind of official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the thing may be done by or before the official` official `an enactment requires or authorizes the thing to be done by or before that kind of official` `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done` MEANS
    IF   `an enactment requires or authorizes the thing to be done by or before that kind of official`
    THEN CONSIDER official
             WHEN `A judge` THEN `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done`
             WHEN `A justice` THEN `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done`
             WHEN `A coroner` THEN `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done`
             WHEN `A public officer` THEN `the official's jurisdiction or powers extend to the place where the thing is to be done`
             WHEN `Another kind of person` THEN `s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer`
    ELSE `s 27(1) speaks only of a thing that an enactment requires or authorizes to be done by or before a judge, justice, coroner or public officer`

-- src:208 | (2) If in an enactment power is given to a person to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, all the powers that are necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are also deemed to be given.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(2) (src:208)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) speaks only of the powers necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(2) speaks only of the powers necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing"

-- src:208 | (2) If in an enactment power is given to a person to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing, all the powers that are necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing are also deemed to be given.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(2) (src:208)
GIVEN `an enactment gives the person power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(2) the power is deemed to be given` `an enactment gives the person power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing` `the power is necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it` MEANS
    IF   `an enactment gives the person power to do or enforce the doing of an act or thing` AND `the power is necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of it`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 27(2) speaks only of the powers necessary to enable the person to do or enforce the doing of the act or thing`

DECLARE `What an enactment confers or imposes` IS ONE OF
    `A power`
    `A duty`
    `Something else`

DECLARE `What s 27(3) says of a power or duty` IS ONE OF
    `The power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires`
    `The duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires`

-- src:209 | (3) If in an enactment a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(3) (src:209)
GIVETH A `What s 27(3) says of a power or duty`
`s 27(3) speaks only of a power conferred or a duty imposed` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(3) speaks only of a power conferred or a duty imposed"

-- src:209 | (3) If in an enactment a power is conferred or a duty imposed, the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(3) (src:209)
GIVEN conferred IS A `What an enactment confers or imposes`
GIVETH A `What s 27(3) says of a power or duty`
`s 27(3) when a power may be exercised or a duty must be performed` conferred MEANS
    CONSIDER conferred
        WHEN `A power` THEN `The power may be exercised from time to time as occasion requires`
        WHEN `A duty` THEN `The duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires`
        WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 27(3) speaks only of a power conferred or a duty imposed`

DECLARE `Something a power to make regulations includes` IS ONE OF
    `Repeal the regulations`
    `Amend the regulations`
    `Make other regulations`
    `Something else`

-- src:210 | (4) If in an enactment a power is conferred to make regulations, the power includes a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal or amend the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(4) (src:210)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(4) speaks only of an enactment that confers a power to make regulations` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(4) speaks only of an enactment that confers a power to make regulations"

-- src:210 | (4) If in an enactment a power is conferred to make regulations, the power includes a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal or amend the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(4) (src:210)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(4) lists what a power to make regulations includes and does not say it includes nothing else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(4) lists what a power to make regulations includes and does not say it includes nothing else"

-- src:210 | (4) If in an enactment a power is conferred to make regulations, the power includes a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal or amend the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(4) (src:210)
GIVEN thing IS A `Something a power to make regulations includes`
      `an enactment confers a power to make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(4) a power to make regulations includes the power` thing `an enactment confers a power to make regulations` MEANS
    IF   `an enactment confers a power to make regulations`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
             WHEN `Repeal the regulations` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Amend the regulations` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Make other regulations` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 27(4) lists what a power to make regulations includes and does not say it includes nothing else`
    ELSE `s 27(4) speaks only of an enactment that confers a power to make regulations`

DECLARE `How a power is exercised` HAS
    `the manner`                          IS A STRING
    `the consent and conditions, if any`  IS A LIST OF STRING

-- "a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any": the included power
-- is exercised as the power to make the regulations is.
-- src:210 | (4) If in an enactment a power is conferred to make regulations, the power includes a power exercisable in the same manner, and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to repeal or amend the regulations and make others.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(4) (src:210)
GIVEN `how the power to make the regulations is exercised` IS A `How a power is exercised`
GIVETH A `How a power is exercised`
`s 27(4) how the included power to repeal, amend or make others is exercised` `how the power to make the regulations is exercised` MEANS
    `how the power to make the regulations is exercised`

DECLARE `Who must do the other act` IS ONE OF
    `The Lieutenant Governor in Council`
    `A public officer`
    `Someone else`

-- src:211 | (5) If in an enactment the doing of an authorized act is dependent on an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer, the Lieutenant Governor in Council or public officer has the power to do that other act or thing.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(5) (src:211)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends"

-- src:211 | (5) If in an enactment the doing of an authorized act is dependent on an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer, the Lieutenant Governor in Council or public officer has the power to do that other act or thing.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(5) (src:211)
GIVEN who IS A `Who must do the other act`
      `the doing of an authorized act is dependent on the other act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(5) the one who must do the other act has the power to do it` who `the doing of an authorized act is dependent on the other act` MEANS
    IF   `the doing of an authorized act is dependent on the other act`
    THEN CONSIDER who
             WHEN `The Lieutenant Governor in Council` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `A public officer` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Someone else` THEN `s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends`
    ELSE `s 27(5) speaks only of an act of the Lieutenant Governor in Council or of a public officer on which an authorized act depends`

DECLARE `Who in an agreement a power to enter into it is about` IS ONE OF
    `The person given the power`
    `The person with whom the agreement is to be made`
    `Someone else`

-- src:212 | (6) Power given to a person in an enactment to enter into an agreement includes the power for the person with whom the agreement is to be made to enter into the agreement and to carry out its terms, subject to conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(6) (src:212)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(6) speaks only of the person given the power to enter into an agreement and the person with whom it is to be made` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 27(6) speaks only of the person given the power to enter into an agreement and the person with whom it is to be made"

-- src:212 | (6) Power given to a person in an enactment to enter into an agreement includes the power for the person with whom the agreement is to be made to enter into the agreement and to carry out its terms, subject to conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 27(6) (src:212)
GIVEN who IS A `Who in an agreement a power to enter into it is about`
      `the conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27(6) the person may enter into the agreement and carry out its terms` who `the conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power are met` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
        WHEN `The person given the power` THEN `the conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power are met`
        WHEN `The person with whom the agreement is to be made` THEN `the conditions that apply to that person in the exercise of the power are met`
        WHEN `Someone else` THEN `s 27(6) speaks only of the person given the power to enter into an agreement and the person with whom it is to be made`

DECLARE `Something a power to inspect or require the production of records includes` IS ONE OF
    `Make copies of the records`
    `Make extracts of the records`
    `Something else`

