    ELSE `s 27(7) speaks only of a power to inspect or to require the production of records`

§ `s 41 Powers to make regulations`

DECLARE `Something a power to make regulations is construed as empowering` IS ONE OF
    `Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it`
        HAS `they are considered necessary and advisable`            IS A BOOLEAN
            `they are ancillary to the enactment`                    IS A BOOLEAN
            `they are not inconsistent with the enactment`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `Provide for administrative and procedural matters for which no express, or only partial, provision has been made`
    `Limit the application of a regulation in time or place or both`
    `Prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment`
    `Provide that contravention of a regulation is an offence`
        HAS `the regulation is made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Provide that a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty`
        HAS `the penalty`                                            IS A NUMBER
            `the greatest penalty the Offence Act provides`          IS A NUMBER
    `Something else`

-- src:422 | 41 (1) If an enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations, the enactment must be construed as empowering the Lieutenant Governor in Council or that other person, for the purpose of carrying out the enactment according to its intent, to
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(1) (src:422)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) speaks only of an enactment that provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(1) speaks only of an enactment that provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations"

-- src:422 | 41 (1) If an enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations, the enactment must be construed as empowering the Lieutenant Governor in Council or that other person, for the purpose of carrying out the enactment according to its intent, to
-- src:423 | (a) make regulations as are considered necessary and advisable, are ancillary to it, and are not inconsistent with it,
-- src:424 | (b) provide for administrative and procedural matters for which no express, or only partial, provision has been made,
-- src:425 | (c) limit the application of a regulation in time or place or both,
-- src:426 | (d) prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment,
-- src:427 | (e) provide, for a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council, that its contravention constitutes an offence, and
-- src:428 | (f) provide that a person who is guilty of an offence created under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty not greater than the penalties provided in the Offence Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(1) (src:422-428)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) lists what a power to make regulations is construed as empowering and does not say it empowers nothing else` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(1) lists what a power to make regulations is construed as empowering and does not say it empowers nothing else"

-- src:423 | (a) make regulations as are considered necessary and advisable, are ancillary to it, and are not inconsistent with it,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(1)(a) (src:423)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it"

-- src:427 | (e) provide, for a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council, that its contravention constitutes an offence, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(1)(e) (src:427)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1)(e) speaks only of a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(1)(e) speaks only of a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council"

-- src:422 | 41 (1) If an enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations, the enactment must be construed as empowering the Lieutenant Governor in Council or that other person, for the purpose of carrying out the enactment according to its intent, to
-- src:423 | (a) make regulations as are considered necessary and advisable, are ancillary to it, and are not inconsistent with it,
-- src:424 | (b) provide for administrative and procedural matters for which no express, or only partial, provision has been made,
-- src:425 | (c) limit the application of a regulation in time or place or both,
-- src:426 | (d) prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment,
-- src:427 | (e) provide, for a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council, that its contravention constitutes an offence, and
-- src:428 | (f) provide that a person who is guilty of an offence created under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty not greater than the penalties provided in the Offence Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(1)(a) to (f) (src:422-428)
GIVEN thing IS A `Something a power to make regulations is construed as empowering`
      `the enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(1) the power to make regulations is construed as empowering` thing `the enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
             WHEN `Make regulations considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it` advisable ancillary consistent THEN
                 IF   advisable AND ancillary AND consistent
                 THEN TRUE
                 ELSE `s 41(1)(a) speaks only of regulations that are considered necessary and advisable, ancillary to the enactment and not inconsistent with it`
             WHEN `Provide for administrative and procedural matters for which no express, or only partial, provision has been made` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Limit the application of a regulation in time or place or both` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Prescribe the amount of a fee authorized by the enactment` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `Provide that contravention of a regulation is an offence` byLGiC THEN
                 IF   byLGiC
                 THEN TRUE
                 ELSE `s 41(1)(e) speaks only of a regulation made by or with the approval of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`
             WHEN `Provide that a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (e) is liable to a penalty` penalty ceiling THEN penalty AT MOST ceiling
             WHEN `Something else` THEN `s 41(1) lists what a power to make regulations is construed as empowering and does not say it empowers nothing else`
    ELSE `s 41(1) speaks only of an enactment that provides that the Lieutenant Governor in Council or any other person may make regulations`

-- src:429 | (2) A regulation made under the authority of an enactment has the force of law.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(2) (src:429)
