`s 41(2) speaks only of a regulation made under the authority of an enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(2) speaks only of a regulation made under the authority of an enactment"

-- src:429 | (2) A regulation made under the authority of an enactment has the force of law.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 41(2) (src:429)
GIVEN `the regulation is made under the authority of an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(2) the regulation has the force of law` `the regulation is made under the authority of an enactment` MEANS
    IF   `the regulation is made under the authority of an enactment`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 41(2) speaks only of a regulation made under the authority of an enactment`
